WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.255
Grandfather looked from Heidi and Clara to Grandmamma.

2
00:00:04.256 --> 00:00:11.568
They were all sitting at the table outside Grandfather's hut and it was time for Clara to get ready to go.

3
00:00:11.569 --> 00:00:16.739
"I've been thinking," Grandfather said to Grandmamma.

4
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:21.075
"If you are willing, Clara can stay here.

5
00:00:21.076 --> 00:00:25.971
We can make a soft bed for her just like Heidi's upstairs."

6
00:00:25.972 --> 00:00:28.581
Grandmamma wasn't sure.

7
00:00:28.582 --> 00:00:33.166
Clara and Heidi watched her eagerly as she thought.

8
00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:39.478
After a pause, she decided it would do no harm for Clara to stay up on the mountain,

9
00:00:39.479 --> 00:00:45.616
and it would be less tiring for her not to be carried up and down from Dorfli every day.

10
00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:53.935
"Your offer is very kind," she said. "I agree."

11
00:00:53.936 --> 00:00:56.398
The girls were overjoyed.

12
00:00:56.399 --> 00:01:04.057
Grandfather set to work making Clara's bed, and Grandmamma made sure she had lots of warm blankets for the night.

13
00:01:04.058 --> 00:01:08.100
They made arrangements for Grandmamma to return in a week.

14
00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:15.328
When the men arrived with Grandmamma's horse, she said goodnight to Grandfather and thanked him again.

15
00:01:15.329 --> 00:01:20.722
"I am sure she will grow stronger here," Grandfather said.

16
00:01:20.723 --> 00:01:26.289
Grandfather woke up early the next morning to prepare a picnic for Clara and Heidi.

17
00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:32.546
He wheeled Clara's chair out in front of the hut and then made them a lunch.

18
00:01:32.547 --> 00:01:40.491
When Peter arrived and saw Clara's wheelchair waiting outside, he knew it meant Clara was coming up the mountain.

19
00:01:40.492 --> 00:01:45.564
He looked around to complain to someone, but no one was around.

20
00:01:45.565 --> 00:01:49.980
In a burst of anger, Peter gave the chair a mighty kick.

21
00:01:49.981 --> 00:01:55.789
It went flying down the mountainside and smashed far below against some rocks.

22
00:01:55.790 --> 00:02:04.237
"Clara will have to go away now," he thought, "and it will be just me and Heidi again."

23
00:02:04.238 --> 00:02:09.076
Inside the hut, Grandfather was feeding the girls breakfast.

24
00:02:09.077 --> 00:02:13.320
Clara finished another big bowlful of the delicious milk.

25
00:02:13.321 --> 00:02:16.476
"It's curious," she said.

26
00:02:16.477 --> 00:02:27.411
"For as long as I can remember, I have eaten only because I had to, but this morning I woke up with a real appetite."

27
00:02:27.412 --> 00:02:32.486
When the three came out of the hut, they could not find Clara's wheelchair.

28
00:02:32.487 --> 00:02:36.066
"It must have been the wind," said Heidi.

29
00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:39.068
"Maybe it rolled down the mountain."

30
00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:43.868
"Now, we won't be able to go," said Clara sadly.

31
00:02:43.869 --> 00:02:49.034
But Grandfather wasn't going to let the two little girls down.

32
00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:52.838
"I can carry Clara on my back this time.

33
00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.691
But where's Peter?

34
00:02:54.692 --> 00:02:57.513
Daisy and Dusky are still here.

35
00:02:57.514 --> 00:03:00.111
We will have to take them with us."

36
00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:07.961
The girls were thrilled with the news, and they all set off up the mountainside with the two happy goats.

37
00:03:07.962 --> 00:03:16.224
Up on the mountain, Heidi found a sunlit spot, and Grandfather settled Clara comfortably onto the grass.

38
00:03:16.225 --> 00:03:21.576
Then, he headed back down to see what he could discover about Clara's wheelchair.

39
00:03:21.577 --> 00:03:26.753
The sky was deep blue and not a single cloud could be seen.

40
00:03:26.754 --> 00:03:33.621
The snow field higher up on the mountain sparkled as if sprinkled with thousands of silver stars.

41
00:03:33.622 --> 00:03:41.097
After chatting happily with Clara for a few hours, Heidi wanted to wander about to pick flowers.

42
00:03:41.098 --> 00:03:47.371
"Would you think me unkind, Clara, if I left you for a few minutes?" asked Heidi.

43
00:03:47.372 --> 00:03:54.366
Clara kindly agreed, and Heidi ran off in search of the brightly colored blossoms she loved.

44
00:03:54.367 --> 00:04:00.858
As Clara rested by herself, she found an unexpected pleasure in sitting all alone.

45
00:04:00.859 --> 00:04:06.145
She picked some fresh grass and waved it at Daisy who was grazing nearby.

46
00:04:06.146 --> 00:04:10.700
"Here Daisy, here Daisy," she called.

47
00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:15.546
The goat wandered over and Clara wiggled the grass under the goat's nose.

48
00:04:15.547 --> 00:04:19.010
Daisy snorted happily and Clara laughed.

49
00:04:19.011 --> 00:04:30.633
For the first time, she felt a great desire to be independent and to be able to help others instead of everyone having to look after her.

